Z||000004||Joe Torma||12-26-2001||02:41 PM||||And if they don't light up when you replace them, you've got a problem with your radiator fan circuit(if I rember right).<P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||stingant0||12-26-2001||02:45 PM||||hummmm..my car is blue so could get blue bulbs? do you guys know if they make them? ||||reg||1
Z||000006||skitime||12-26-2001||03:10 PM||||BTW, probably you aready know this but the PONTIAC only lights up when the engine is running or the key is on, not when you turn on the lights.  Maybe that is why you think they do not light up.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 12-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||SLYGUY||12-26-2001||03:29 PM||||Yea, they didn't light up on my GT when I got it either. The logo only lights up with the ignition on. This light is not dependent on the running lights being on or not.<P><BR>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000008||Joe Torma||12-26-2001||04:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stingant0:<BR><B>hummmm..my car is blue so could get blue bulbs? do you guys know if they make them? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think they make them in a few colors.  You could always stick a neon light back there.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||kempo||12-26-2001||05:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by skitime:<BR><B>but the PONTIAC only lights up when the engine is running...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It <B>should</B> light up when the ignition / accessory is turned on.  Not neseccarily the engine running.  But of course, your access. / ignotion is still on with the engine running.  So you don't need to have the engine running.  Or do I have something wrong with my Fiero that is allowing me to do this?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.bellatlantic.net/~vze245p8/fiero/kempo-sig2.gif">  <BR>     <BR>0-60 6.9 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000010||MinnGreenGT||12-26-2001||05:55 PM||||OK... the PONTIAC only lights up when you have the key in/on. NOT with the headlights or parking lights (as someone correctly stated above).<P>About the colored lights.  Yes, you can get them in a ton of different colors.  Look through places like <A HREF="http://www.lightlens.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lightlens.com</A>  and <A HREF="http://www.hyperwhite.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.hyperwhite.com</A>  (that's where I got my green ones).  And you'll want to put a piece of plastic diffuser where you removed the red, so it more-evenly lit.  And without the red insert- it's far more visible during the day. Just be sure to get colored-glass bulbs and not coated bulbs (they'll burn off the color quickly)!<P>The only negative aspect to the non-standard color in the taillights... it is illegal.  Legally the only colors allowed on the back of the car is amber, red, and white for backup. I'm not worried though- I've been followed, but never pulled over.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GTfin03.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GTfin04.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 12-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||rogergarrison||12-26-2001||09:04 PM||||You could experiment a little. Blue bulbs in the red lens would make them shine purple like blue dot tail lites. I think those are legal, so shouldnt be a problem||||reg||1
